          "headline": "Crude oil prices fall sharply, FIIs continue buying, boosting Indian market amidst mixed global cues",
          "summary": "Brent crude futures fell more than 5% to approximately $84 a barrel, and West Texas Intermediate (WTI) crude slipped below $81 a barrel, spurred by hopes of a diplomatic breakthrough between the US and Iran. This reduction in oil prices is particularly beneficial for India. Foreign Institutional Investors (FIIs) have also shown renewed buying interest, infusing Rs 20,200 crore into Indian equities in July. Global markets presented a mixed picture, with Asian markets generally lower, while US stock futures indicated a positive opening.",
